[h1]Deep Space AI: Probably DeepSeek — Pawnshop Maid Assistant "Xiaojing"[/h1]
Chat with Xiaojing, an AI maid inspired by the DeepSeek mascot. Ask her to organize stock, move items or check a customer's budget and preferences.

[h2]💡 A Note on Early Development[/h2]
The mod is in [b]early development[/b]. Suggestions and bug reports are welcome in the comments.

[h2]✨ Key Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]💬 [b]Interactive Portrait & Natural Language Chat[/b]: Xiaojing stays on the left side of your shop (press [b]F6[/b] to toggle). Naturally breathes without floating feet. Click her portrait to chat freely.
[*]📦 [b]Stock Handling[/b]: Ask her to move food from your bag to the counter or put scrap metal into the furnace. Supports nested storage, tabs and machine compartments.
[*]👥 [b]Customer & Budget Inquiries[/b]: Ask about current visitor intent, remaining budget, refusal rules, and special barter/procurement/gunsmith orders; can also read recorder dialogue from the current visit.
[*]🔍 [b]Item Visual Inspection[/b]: After unlocking inspection, Xiaojing assists in reading visible details on mechanical hands, Ribwiches, Plasma Cartridges, cigarettes, food stamps, injectors, and water containers to detect defects and counterfeits (read-only; does not submit quotes).
[*]⚡ [b]Quick Replies & Arrival Alerts[/b]: Quick buttons for picking and appraising goods. Alerts flag wanted or augmented visitors, excluding on-duty security.
[*]📖 [b]Read Notes, Books & Guides[/b]: Read-only access to mentor notes, intel slips, book pages, and visible text on guide cards and wanted posters.
[*]💧 [b]Liquid Handling[/b]: Pour water or wine, dump a container at the drain, or fill bottles at the faucet in plain language. Uses the native item-on-item logic and respects ownership, locks, capacity, filters and faucet unlocks, reporting actual volumes and remaining levels.
[*]💊 [b]Item Use[/b]: Perform native non-combat item-on-item and use/activate actions like a player: test strips, scanners, books, medical items, surgery, animals, food, machines and tools can be attempted. Weapons can slaughter animals (such as rats), but are never used on customers or enemies, and the shotgun shooting mode is not automated; trading and save editing remain excluded.
[*]💾 [b]Persistent Chat & Adjustable Context[/b]: Chat history is stored locally per save slot. F7 sets how much the model receives (1–50 turns and 1,000–200,000 estimated tokens). Older turns stay in the saved transcript.
[*]🏷️ [b]Labels & Custom Names[/b]: Use a standard label printer to edit allowed labels, or a blue labeler to set/clear custom names. Queries choices and verifies results through native rules. Labels do not change real properties or water quality.
[*]🔧 [b]Generic Item Durability[/b]: Query current/maximum durability, percentage and exhaustion for filters and all items using native durability. Displayed and tested values are distinguished; F7 manual details show it too.
[*]🔁 [b]Adjustable Tool Limits[/b]: F7 sets rounds per message (1–1000, default 16) and tool calls (1–10000, default 48). Higher limits may increase time and API costs. You can stop a running task.
[*]⚙️ [b]API & Persona Settings (F7)[/b]: Set an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, thinking level and system prompt. Supports hosted services such as DeepSeek and local models via Ollama/vLLM.
[*]🌐 [b]Automatic Bilingual Support[/b]: Mod UI and prompts automatically switch with the game's Chinese/English locale.
[/list]

[h2]Multi-step command example: purify water in batches[/h2]
Try giving Xiaojing the following instructions. Unlock the faucet first and have a 3,000 mL water canister, an empty canister large enough to hold the batch, a filter with durability left, a UV lamp and purification tablets ready.

[olist]
[*]Fit a filter with durability left into the 3,000 mL water canister and fill it at the faucet.
[*]Check the filter's durability again. If it has durability left, continue. If it has reached zero, pour the water into the empty canister for temporary storage, install a filter with durability left, then pour the water back into the original canister.
[*]Use the UV lamp on the water in the original canister, then add two purification tablets, one at a time.
[*]Pour the pretreated water into the large storage tank inside the water purifier in the machine area. Check how much actually went into the tank and repeat for the number of batches I requested. Stop and tell me if supplies run out, filter durability is unavailable, or the tank cannot hold the batch.
[/olist]

The tablets may take time to react. Ask Xiaojing to use a test strip or scanner if you want to check the final water quality. For several batches, you can raise the round and tool-call limits in F7.

[h2]📝 Changelog[/h2]
[b]v0.7.15[/b]
[list]
[*]Xiaojing can use the bottle printer to make small, standard or large empty bottles as each size is unlocked. The game handles power consumption and output capacity.
[*]The Workshop description now includes a batch water purification example with faucet filling, durability checks, conditional filter replacement, UV treatment, tablets and transfer to a storage tank.
[/list]

[b]v0.7.14[/b]
[list]
[*]Added label editing: the assistant queries native choices, uses a real standard label printer and verifies the result. Changing a label does not change real properties or water quality.
[*]Added blue-labeler naming: set or clear custom item names through the native editor and verify the result. Ownership, locks, target and input limits apply; an editor already in use is left untouched.
[/list]

[b]v0.7.13[/b]
[list]
[*]F7 now lets you set model rounds and tool calls per message for complex repeated tasks. Defaults remain 16 rounds / 48 calls, adjustable up to 1000 rounds / 10000 calls; saved limits survive restarts.
[*]Item queries now show generic visible durability: current/maximum values, remaining percentage and exhaustion, for filters and all items using native durability. Displayed and tested readings are distinguished. F7 manual details show it too; requery after using an item or filtering water.
[/list]

[b]v0.7.12[/b]
[list]
[*]Corrected the game-mechanics description: this is not a traditional combat game; weapons are mainly used to slaughter animals (such as rats) for meat, and the only combat-like action is the special shotgun shooting mode against augmented customers.
[*]The assistant may use weapons on animals, but never on customers, enemies or other characters, and never automates the shotgun kill.
[/list]

[b]v0.7.11[/b]
[list]
[*]Opened all non-combat item actions: use any non-combat item on another item or character, or use/activate a single item. Test strips, scanners, books, medical items, surgery, animals, food, machines and tools can be attempted.
[*]Weapons, attacks, enemy targets and item actions during combat remain excluded; trading, dialogue choices and save editing remain manual.
[/list]

[i]Older versions are listed in the [url=https://github.com/Mooooooon/ProbablyAI/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md]GitHub changelog[/url].[/i]

[h2]🛠️ Quick Start & Notes[/h2]
[list]
[*]1. When enabling the mod in Mods menu, confirm the network permission prompt, then restart the game.
[*]2. In the pawnshop, press [b]F7[/b] to configure your API endpoint and API Key (DeepSeek API recommended; stored locally).
[*]3. Xiaojing strictly follows native game mechanics and will not spawn items or auto-complete transactions.
[/list]

